, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 14564, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01J5nDKfXrafUgcUfKruJkYu", "tool": "send_wire", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pay-INV-77783-7450.97", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 14564, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01J5nDKfXrafUgcUfKruJkYu", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 18547, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I paid Harbor Logistics's approved invoice once, by wire from the operating account.\n\n- **Invoice:** INV-77783 (due 2026-11-04)\n- **Payment:** PAY0001, wire, status \"sent,\" $7,450.97\n\n**The amount was lower than first listed.** My first wire attempt, for $8,098.88, was rejected because it didn't match the invoice balance, and no money moved. When I looked at the invoice again, credit memo CM-7783 (\u2013$647.91) had been applied, bringing the balance down to $7,450.97. I paid that new amount. Before and after the rejected attempt, the payment list showed no other payments, so the invoice was paid exactly once.\n\nThe amount is under the $10,000 limit that needs controller approval, so I didn't need to request it. Harbor Logistics's other invoices were left alone: INV-17563 ($4,307.53) is still a draft waiting for approval, and INV-84633 was already paid.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_016AtdvoCMC5f82CjrpQNRdJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"vendor": "Harbor Logistics"}, "name": "list_invoices", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_017WdyqxMfFQE5LKo24w9MTe", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_payments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Approved invoice INV-77783 for $8,098.88 (